**/target
**/Cargo.lock
# The server's lock — the one at the root — IS committed. Most of its dependencies are spelled `"*"`, so
# with the lock ignored a release resolves fresh and takes the newest semver-compatible release of every
# transitive crate in a ~400-crate graph: the same tag built twice would be two different binaries, and
# one bad patch published anywhere would break a release that changed nothing. Committed, a release is
# what was tested here, and a broken transitive dependency reproduces locally instead of only in CI.
#
# The client's lock (`ui/`) and the wire crate's (`shared/`) stay ignored: neither is built by CI — the
# browser bundle is built on a developer's machine and committed as `wwwroot/`.
!/Cargo.lock
**/dist
.claude
.idea
.DS_Store
.mcp.json
